# NOT `node_modules/`. A trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY only, so a symlink or a plain
# file of that name is left untracked-but-not-ignored and `git add -A` stages it. One did:
# a committed `node_modules` symlink dangles on a runner and `pnpm install` then fails at
# `mkdir node_modules` with ENOTDIR, taking down every job before a test runs. Without the
# slash the real directory is still ignored, at any depth.
node_modules
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
coverage/
.turbo/
*.local
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
playwright-report/
test-results/
.vite/
